        "first_change_on_file_history": {
          "author_date": "2026-10-17T22:05:58-04:00",
          "commit": "cf3e93860996c08f18c7598c99b00bd296e23f41",
          "message": "Pass 12004: the bare CP-real theta quark sector cannot fit -- with Pass 12005 the vectorlike row is necessary as well as sufficient, so with exact CP the theta flavour chain is a Nelson-Barr theory (Claude track). On the theta-group generalised-CP locus (Re tau, Re tau_d in Z; Omega12 and the 5bar Wilson line imaginary mod Z/6) both theta Yukawas satisfy Y = Ph o conj(Y) with a common left factor e^{2 pi i a^2/3} (120 points to 5e-11; off-locus control 1e-2), so J = 0 identically and tree-level theta-bar in {0, pi}. The up sector fits exactly there (Weber point tau = 1 + 0.8745i); at that tau a complex down sector fits exactly (positive control), but the bare CP-real down sector does not: a full grid of 746,496 points with a centred-window theta accurate in the cusp (validated to 2e-13) gives global chi2 = 329 for 5 observables and 3 parameters; the Codex 12005 bare point scores 2.5e5; letting tau move gives at best 213 at the cost of the up sector. Two corrections along the way are recorded: a 'robust' minimum that was a shared basin, and an N=40 deep-cusp value (257) that was a truncation artefact (357). Any CP-invariant moduli potential is stationary across the locus (Palais symmetric criticality; transverse gradients 5e-9 vs 65). Scope: T^2-type gCP, 11942 down model, search-based. Search drivers and run records in analysis/search_drivers_12004/. Forty Points sentence and ledger row."
        },
        "most_recent_change_on_file_history": {
          "author_date": "2026-10-18T19:24:27-04:00",
          "commit": "b8a3c339b2c1a1fc992267529de24dad7b92dd8d",
          "message": "Pass 12049: the coloured threshold inventory for the 11950 strong-CP divisor -- a hypercharge Wilson line restoring SU(5) at Omega_12 = 0 gives XY (-4) + one vectorlike 5+5bar (+1) = -3, exactly the 3/2 log chi10 that regularity needs; the one pair is the single Nelson-Barr row, and its hypercharge masses give the 2/3 lepton Clebsch (Claude track; conditional on the identification)"
        },
