          "commit": "dbe3a4117d2afe5d2f96f53e4ae61d1711a452e2",
          "message": "Pass 11938: the second small parameter and the Weber law for the up texture. Every tangent direction orthogonal to the stabiliser state (the polar line, any magic) maps the E8 Cartan vev into the reducible locus: the theta Yukawa is exactly rank one (11936's 'locked deep cusp' was rank one). Off it by theta = arcsin|u1| the spectrum is (1, A theta t, B theta^2 t) -- a geometric texture carried by Omega12 (cites 11912). The heat-equation expansion about a product torus gives the Omega12-independent law m_u m_t/m_c^2 = |f(tau1) f(tau2)|^8/4 (Weber f; per factor |eta(t)^2/(eta(t/2)eta(2t))|^8/sqrt2; checked to 3e-8): 4 for two square tori, 2^(2/3) for two hexagonal, >= 1 for any CM elliptic-point product. Data 0.54: CM excluded; E8 cusp regime excluded (search floor R >= 0.80/t over all directions); reachable at most at t = O(1), where the inversion is branch-dependent. Forty Points sentence and ledger row (Claude track)"
